    "english":  "The bee, covered with the fragrant golden pollen of the wild pidavu\nwhose petals are marked with crimson lines like red lac on white conch,\nshines bright as gold rubbed upon a touchstone on the green hill!\nYesterday, the lord of these fertile mountains came to our millet field\nand helped us scare away the parrots, seeking an opportunity to speak.\nFinding no chance to whisper his heart to me, he departed with a lingering look.\nHis departure did not grieve me, my beloved companion;\nwhat torments my memory now is my own unkind deedΓÇö\nhow, seeing him stand there gazing with insatiable desire like a bee\nthat hovers over a blossom yet does not drink,\nI cruelly turned away and tightened the bracelets upon my arms!",
